      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): resolve legacy modelstudio profile aliases",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nLegacy explicit auth profile ids like modelstudio:default fail to resolve after provider canonicalization to qwen, causing valid stored credentials to be ignored and agent turns to fail with No credentials found for profile \\\"modelstudio:default\\\".\n\n## Summary\n- resolve explicit legacy provider-prefixed profile ids through provider auth aliases when direct lookup misses\n- preserve explicit profile precedence: if modelstudio:default exists directly, use it instead of alias fallback\n- add focused regression coverage for both fallback path and precedence path\n\n## Evidence\n- Repro: before this change, resolving { provider: \"modelstudio\", profileId: \"modelstudio:default\" } with only qwen:default in store throws No credentials found for profile \"modelstudio:default\".\n- Validation: after change, same setup resolves to qwen:default and returns the expected key\n- Guardrail: explicit modelstudio:default credential remains preferred when both modelstudio:default and qwen:default exist\n- Local test run:\n  - [x] pnpm exec vitest run src/agents/model-auth.profiles.test.ts -t \"84081|modelstudio profile\"\n\nRelated: #84081\r\n",
        "branch": "fix/84081-modelstudio-profile-alias-repro",
